@page
@model PersonalTools.Pages.PrivacyModel
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy"; }

<div class="container px-3 px-lg-4"><div class="row justify-content-center"><div class="col-12 col-lg-8">
    <p class="eyebrow">Last updated: 2 September 2026</p><h1 class="page-title">Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle section-spacing">How Personal Tools and Case Tycoon use and protect your information.</p>
    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm"><div class="card-body p-4 p-lg-5">
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Who is responsible</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Jake Hutson operates Personal Tools and Case Tycoon and is the data controller for the personal information described here. Questions and privacy requests can be sent to <a href="mailto:nerb162@gmail.com">nerb162@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Information collected</h2><p class="small-muted mb-2">For registered accounts, the service stores your email address, display name, securely hashed password, account role and—only when you choose to link it—your SteamID.</p><p class="small-muted mb-0">For browser-based Case Tycoon accounts, the service stores your chosen username, an internal account identifier, gameplay progress, inventory, battle activity, achievements, preferences, friendships and pending friend requests. For all accounts it stores authentication-session details such as expiry and browser user-agent. Limited technical information, including IP addresses, request details and errors, may appear in security and operational logs.</p></section>
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Why information is used</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Account, session and gameplay data provide the service you request and preserve your progress. Security and operational data help prevent misuse, investigate faults and protect accounts. The lawful bases relied on are performance of the service requested by you and legitimate interests in operating, securing and improving the service. Personal information is not used for advertising or sold.</p></section>
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Case Tycoon guest access</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">A guest account is linked to an encrypted authentication cookie in the browser that created it. Guest sessions can last up to 180 days. Clearing site data, changing browser or losing the device may remove access because guest accounts do not have an email recovery method. Case Tycoon uses virtual items and virtual balances only; it does not accept stakes, provide cash-out, or award items with real-world value.</p></section>
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Content and external services</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">The service stores content you deliberately add to its tools. Audio Studio processes selected media entirely in your browser. When you request Steam linking, inventory lookup, Leetify match data, public statistics, prices or other public content, the relevant identifier or request is sent to that provider under its own privacy terms.</p></section>
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Sharing</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Information is shared only with hosting, database and infrastructure providers needed to operate the service, with external services you actively ask the site to contact, or where disclosure is required by law. The service does not use advertising networks, analytics trackers or social-media tracking pixels.</p></section>
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Retention and security</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Account and tool data are kept while the account remains active or until deletion is requested, subject to any limited period needed for security, backups or legal obligations. Ordinary server sessions expire after one day, Remember me sessions after up to 14 days, and guest sessions after up to 180 days. Operational logs are retained only as long as reasonably needed for security and fault investigation. Passwords are never stored in plain text. Controls include HTTPS, encrypted HttpOnly cookies, server-side session validation, access policies, request-forgery protection, rate limiting and security headers.</p></section>
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Your rights</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">Depending on the circumstances, you may request access, correction, deletion, restriction or portability of your information, or object to processing based on legitimate interests. Contact the controller above. You may also complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.</p></section>
        <section class="mb-4"><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Automated decisions and children</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">The service does not make decisions about people that produce legal or similarly significant effects. Case Tycoon is a fan-made simulator and is not real-money gambling. If you are responsible for a child using the service, supervise their use and contact the controller if their information should be removed.</p></section>
        <section><h2 class="h5 fw-semibold">Cookies and browser storage</h2><p class="small-muted mb-0">See the <a asp-page="/Cookies">Cookies page</a> for the storage used by the service and how to change your preferences.</p></section>
    </div></div>
</div></div></div>
